{
  "$schema": "node_modules/wrangler/config-schema.json",
  "main": ".open-next/worker.js",
  "name": "forthe22",
  "compatibility_date": "2026-08-19",
  "compatibility_flags": ["nodejs_compat", "global_fetch_strictly_public"],
  "assets": {
    "directory": ".open-next/assets",
    "binding": "ASSETS"
  },
  "observability": {
    "logs": {
      "enabled": true
    }
  },
  "services": [
    {
      "binding": "WORKER_SELF_REFERENCE",
      "service": "forthe22"
    }
  ],
  /**
   * Non-secret runtime vars — see src/lib/launch-gate.ts and README's
   * "Pre-Launch Gate" section. Committed here (not just set via the
   * Cloudflare dashboard) because `wrangler deploy`/`opennextjs-cloudflare
   * deploy` uploads a version's full var set from this file each time —
   * a dashboard-only edit gets silently wiped by the next deploy from any
   * machine. To flip a flag: edit here, then `npm run deploy`. WHOOP_CLIENT_ID
   * lives here rather than as a `wrangler secret` because it's not actually
   * sensitive — it's already visible in the browser-facing WHOOP OAuth
   * redirect URL (see src/app/api/whoop/authorize/route.ts) — and a
   * dashboard-only value for it hit this exact wipe-on-deploy bug once
   * already, silently breaking the live training snapshot.
   *
   * NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL/NEXT_PUBLIC_CAMPAIGN_URL hit the identical bug: the
   * GitHub Actions workflow passes them as build-time shell env vars, but
   * OpenNext-for-Cloudflare reads NEXT_PUBLIC_* server-side from the Worker's
   * *runtime* env bindings, not just build-time inlining — so a stale
   * dashboard-set NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL ("https://www.forthe22.org", a
   * subdomain with no DNS record) kept silently surviving every deploy,
   * breaking every server-rendered "back to For The 22" link and
   * metadataBase-derived URL site-wide despite the workflow's env block
   * always looking correct. Declared here now so a deploy always sets the
   * real value, the same fix already applied once for WHOOP_CLIENT_ID.
   *
   * Values that are actually sensitive (SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY,
   * WHOOP_CLIENT_SECRET, PREVIEW_ACCESS_TOKEN, the analytics API token,
   * etc.) do NOT belong here — they're pushed as Worker *secret* bindings
   * by the "Sync Worker secrets" step in
   * .github/workflows/deploy.yml on every deploy, sourced from GitHub
   * Actions repo secrets, so they get the same "never dashboard-only"
   * guarantee without committing the values to git.
   */
  "vars": {
    "SITE_LIVE": "true",
    "CAMPAIGN_LIVE": "false",
    "WHOOP_CLIENT_ID": "fc3a41a2-08c9-4141-b5bb-35773f4c3509",
    "NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL": "https://forthe22.org",
    "NEXT_PUBLIC_CAMPAIGN_URL": "https://tri.forthe22.org"
  }
}
